# --- Authentication and persistence (Phase 3) --------------------------
# Argon2id password hashing (argon2-cffi is pinned above as a runtime dep).
# JWT access tokens, per-IP rate limiting, and account/session storage.
#
# DEVIATION (documented in docs/PHASE_3_EVIDENCE.md): the execution guide names
# `python-jose[cryptography]`. It was installed, audited, and rejected because
# it pulls in `ecdsa`, which carries CVE-2024-23342 (Minerva timing attack on
# P-256) with **no fix version and no planned fix** - the project considers
# side-channel attacks out of scope. PyJWT provides the HS256 signing this
# phase needs, has no `ecdsa` dependency, and leaves pip-audit clean. Shipping
# a known-unfixable cryptographic vulnerability would violate the Phase 3
# dependency rule and the project's supply-chain requirements (SUPPLY-002).
